# Worked Example {#appendix-example}

This non-normative diagnostic example elides certificates, signatures, and
nested token bytes. The requested OID `1.3.6.1.4.1.42623.1.4` is shown only for
review of the proposed profile encoding; it remains pending OCP approval. Exact
detached Claims-Set vectors follow the diagnostic form.

~~~ cbor-diag
602([
  <<61(18([
    <<{
      1: -35,
      3: "application/eat+cwt",
      34: [-43,
        h'6be9f10e1e9388b0f70028b060dc215a0dc4f1b2d60b407689465be40d6e1a28e31e3d7186968eac00ea97db833d715c']
    }>>,
    {33: h'<Lead Attester certificate>'},
    <<{
      10: h'000102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f101112131415161718191a1b1c1d1e1f',
      256: h'0111111111111111111111111111111111',
