The deterministic encoding of the complete `env.nic.0` Claims-Set is:

~~~ hex
a119012b83781e6170706c69636174696f6e2f7370646d2d65766964656e6365\
2b63626f7253824812010000aabbccdd4830820100deadbeef04
~~~

Its SHA-384 digest is
`c322d4b38698e2a652dec5ef6c9158a1f5c654e415870d9a`
`accd3ae367be72bb5d5260f3433b93502a30fd858fb76746`.

For device-emitted EAT, the synthetic CWT bytes are
`d83dd28440a04040`. The deterministic Claims-Set encoding is:

~~~ hex
a119012b83736170706c69636174696f6e2f6561742b63777448d83dd28440a0\
404004
~~~

Its SHA-384 digest is
`dd4e41442e3bb7b38fc05437cc9dae0b3e7a7188f37c8030`
`7f5502d5c3e38b96f88c0666707c947a352c092d58974f2c`.

For recursive composition, the synthetic child bundle contains the same CWT
bytes and one detached `env.leaf.0` SPDM Claims-Set. The deterministic parent
Claims-Set encoding is:

~~~ hex
a119012b8378186170706c69636174696f6e2f6561742d62756e2b63626f7258\
55d9025a8248d83dd28440a04040a16a656e762e6c6561662e30583aa119012b\
83781e6170706c69636174696f6e2f7370646d2d65766964656e63652b63626f\
7253824812010000aabbccdd4830820100deadbeef0404
~~~

Its SHA-384 digest is
`41a15dc29c5be302be56efcd77a2d63afa7befdacf28115b`
`35afbca6fcab5d0701201ccdfd9e766246457ba0afaf9e27`.

The native evidence values in these vectors are synthetic and are not valid
signatures or complete protocol responses. The encodings and digests are exact
conformance vectors for the CMW, detached Claims-Set, and digest boundaries.

# Collected CDDL {#appendix-cddl}

The following CDDL collects the profile grammar. The external
`concise-evidence-map` type is defined by
[@{tcg-dice-concise-evidence-binding-for-spdm}] and is required when
validating the collected grammar. `profile-oid` accepts a PEN-relative OID
structure while the requested OID remains pending. After OCP approves the
assignment, it MUST be narrowed to the exact assigned OID encoding.

```include {.small}
!include cddl/composite_eat_ocp_profile.cddl
```
